    "problem_statement": "Duration addition produces incorrect results\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen adding Duration objects to dates/datetimes or other Duration objects, the calculations are producing incorrect results. The addition operation appears to be performing subtraction instead of addition in some cases.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom isodate import Duration\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\n# Duration + Duration should add components\ndur1 = Duration(years=1, months=2)\ndur2 = Duration(years=3, months=4)\nresult = dur1 + dur2\nprint(f\"Expected: P4Y6M, Got: {result}\")\n\n# Duration + date should add to the date\nstart_date = date(2020, 1, 15)\nduration = Duration(years=1, months=6)\nresult = start_date + duration\nprint(f\"Expected: 2021-07-15, Got: {result}\")\n\n# Duration + timedelta should combine properly\nduration = Duration(years=1)\ntd = timedelta(days=30)\nresult = duration + td\nprint(f\"Expected duration with 1 year + 30 days, Got: {result}\")\n```\n\nThe operations are returning unexpected results where addition seems to behave like subtraction."
